                                "sense_id": "1db246dd-b165-30a4-bb54-9b8ccd5aba90",
                                "text": "At the radiant point itself, it was a subject of general remark, the meteors appeared trainless, and shone out for a moment like so many stars..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1da35e9c-8838-490a-b332-01c06da7d10f",
                                "sense_id": "1db246dd-b165-30a4-bb54-9b8ccd5aba90",
                                "text": "Mr Ray Buckton, the Aslef boss, is as miserable as most trainless commuters, though most of the public sees him as the villain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f234160-03a1-420f-a6d3-ef75b9beff95",
                                "sense_id": "1db246dd-b165-30a4-bb54-9b8ccd5aba90",
                                "text": "The silk and satin dresses—all sleeveless, trainless, and above the ankle—spun out a lightness, a feeling of romance and hope."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "254243d3-62ad-49c6-b555-6276b18c6211",
                                "sense_id": "1db246dd-b165-30a4-bb54-9b8ccd5aba90",
                                "text": "There is a bittersweet finality to ending our tour at Burnham-on-Sea, and a distinct end-of-an-era feeling that comes with a visit to the now-trainless and steamer-less, quaint seaside town."
                            }
